  "description": "3 x fig trees: crown reduce to approx. 0.5m-1.0m above the previous reduction points, retaining the 0.5-10m lengths in order to retain a leafy character and develop a new crown structure.  Lift to 5m over the road (minimising pruning wounds as much as possible whilst ensuring adequate clearance) and prune back from property as required to give clearance of 2-3m.  Remove epicormic growth up to 2.5m.  Reduce single scaffold limb on easternmost tree, growing towards neighbours property, by 1-2m below the previous reduction points to reduce end weight over decay at base of limb, pruning back to suitable growth points.\r",
